w your detailed tuition account in Student Center.\n\ud83d\udcb0 Funding Sources\nStudents receive an annual funding package, which may include:\nWestern Graduate Research Scholarship (WGRS)\nGraduate Teaching Assistantship (GTA)\nGraduate Research Fellowship - supervisor stipend (GRF)\n\u23f3 Guaranteed Funding Duration (academic progression and eligibility requirements must be maintained)\nMSc Students: 6 terms (2 years)\nPhD Students: 12 terms (4 years)\nPhD (Transfer & Direct Entry): 15 terms (5 years)\n\ud83d\udcca Budget Planning\nUse the Graduate Student Affordability Calculator to estimate:\nTuition & fees\nHousing\nFood\nOther living expenses\n\ud83d\udd0d Important Notes\nFrom your funding package total, you are expected to pay tuition and ancillary fees.\nYour funding package depends on your supervisor\u2019s home department or faculty.\nStudents in the same lab typically receive similar base funding.\nFunding levels vary across faculties and departments (see 'Student Funding Packages').\n\ud83d\udce9 Questions? Email: neuroscience@uwo.ca\nGraduate\nFuture Students\nAdvisory Committee\nChange of Registration\nCollaborative Specializations\nComprehensive Assessment\nCourses and Milestones\nGraduate Student Life\nResearch Themes\nStudent Funding & Tuition\nStudent Funding Packages\nScholarships & Awards\nReceiving Payments\nFinancial Assistance\nStudent Seminars\nSupervision Handbook\nPolicies and Guidelines\nVisiting Research Students\n\u00a9 1878 - Western University\nNeuroscience\nWestern Interdisciplinary Research Building, WIRB 3168\nLondon, Ontario, Canada, N6A 3K7\nTel: 519.661.4039\nneuroscience@uwo.ca\nPrivacy |\nWeb Standards |\nTerms of Use |\nAccessibility\nKey Topics:\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nResearch\nPeople\nAbout Us\nPopular Resources:\nBMSc Program\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Timetable\nSchulich Medicine & Dentistry Research Office\nDiversity, Equity Statement\nLiving in London", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://www.schulich.uwo.ca/